guamp: heap sizes from the runtime, and metal2vulkan runtime patch 0023 (UniXNU/AdrenoMetal adc18c5 bridge/patches/0023, aff537e)

Adds bridge/patches/0023-heap-texture-size-a-multiple-of-its-alignment.patch: a heap texture's size is a multiple of its alignment
(Turnip 4 KiB against Metal's 128 bytes), so a heap sized as the sum of its textures' sizes holds them (OutOfMemory(Heap) in
SpringBoard and Core Image). 2ff4be9 does not answer heapTextureSizeAndAlignWithDescriptor:/heapBufferSizeAndAlignWithLength:options:
itself (_MTLDevice's answers do not match the runtime's placements), so the frontend gets aff537e's two methods and the bridge its
nmb_device_heap_texture_size_and_align / nmb_device_heap_buffer_size_and_align exports.

